            "text": "{\n  \"relation\": \"REFINED\",\n  \"consensus_summary\": \"In apocalyptic literature, a beast primarily symbolizes an oppressive, anti-God political power, worldly empire, or tyrannical ruler (such as the Antichrist), with some alternative views recognizing it as a symbol for Gentile nations or mere human irrationality.\",\n  \"book_summary\": \"A beast symbolizes a nation or kingdom of the world, serving as the wild, predatory figure of a people, with unclean beasts specifically representing Gentile nations.\",\n  \"consensus_core_identification\": \"Worldly empires, kingdoms, or oppressive political rulers.\",\n  \"book_core_identification\": \"Nations or kingdoms of the world, including Gentile peoples.\",\n  \"core_relation\": \"EQUIVALENT\",\n  \"extension_relation\": \"BOOK_SUPERSET\",\n  \"boundary_disagreement\": \"The consensus primarily restricts the symbolic meaning of 'beast' to specific persecuting, anti-God empires found in apocalyptic texts (Daniel, Revelation). The book broadens this definition to encompass worldly nations and kingdoms in general, specifically including the Gentile nations as a class (applying the vision of Acts 10).\",\n  \"material_contradiction\": \"None. The book's definition aligns with the consensus that Daniel's beasts represent kingdoms, but it elevates the alternative consensus view regarding Acts 10 (Gentiles) into its primary definition.\",\n  \"rationale\": \"Both the book and the consensus identify the beast as a symbol for kingdoms and empires, supported explicitly by Daniel 7:17. The book refines this consensus by removing the strict eschatological and anti-Christian limitations, broadening the referent to any 'nation or kingdom of the world' and explicitly incorporating the Gentile nations (Acts 10) as part of the primary symbolic framework.\",\n  \"citation_support\": \"STRONG\",\n  \"strongest_objection\": \"The apocalyptic beasts in Revelation and Daniel are depicted specifically as demonic or fiercely anti-God powers, not merely as general representations of any worldly nation or the Gentiles.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\"\n}",
